From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 154/342] BSerialPort: NumCharsAvailable() says how many

It was a stub that always gave 0; it asks the driver (FIONREAD) now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kits/device/SerialPort.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kits/device/SerialPort.cpp b/src/kits/device/SerialPort.cpp
index b84899d4d1..e37535492e 100644
--- a/src/kits/device/SerialPort.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/device/SerialPort.cpp
@@ -390,13 +390,15 @@ BSerialPort::SetRTS(bool asserted)
 status_t
 BSerialPort::NumCharsAvailable(int32 *numChars)
 {
-	//No help from the BeBook...
 	if (ffd < 0)
 		return B_NO_INIT;
 
-	// TODO: Implement ?
+	// the bytes a read could take now
+	int size;
+	if (ioctl(ffd, FIONREAD, &size, sizeof(size)) < 0)
+		return errno;
 	if (numChars)
-		*numChars = 0;
+		*numChars = size;
 	return B_OK;
 }
 
